\nAlternatively, I could report confidence as ~0.95-0.97. Let me code this up properly.\n\nAlso, update the evidence string generation (currently it hard-codes the GKN1/CLDN18 text — this is specific to this run; since I've verified it, it's acceptable, but let me make the evidence string mostly generic yet concrete). In fact, this script is the artifact for this specific dataset, so having specific evidence text is fine, but it should be computed rather than hard-coded where possible. I'll write the evidence string programmatically from the top genes of the two sets (highest cross-column CPM ratio).\n\nFurthermore, in report.md I need to include:\n- Task, data, methods (GTF parsing, chunk mapping, promoter bins, CPM, z+rank scoring, swap score definition).\n- Results: T matrix, ranked pairs, top pair statistics, margin, mutual best, LOO stability, correction consistency.\n- Key evidence genes and CPM tables: CLDN18, GKN1, CHIA, CCKAR, SLC26A9 (Stomach markers → Cloaca column); CDX2, CDX4, REG4, ALPI, CD8B, PRF1 (Cloaca/caudal markers → Stomach column).\n- Explain why other candidates fail (Bladder↔Gill: negative reverse direction; gill signal = branchial muscle/cartilage cross-reactivity; bladder set is uninformative).\n- Limitations (sparse ortholog annotation, paralog noise, weak sets for some organs).\n- A note on correlation context.\n- Conclusion: swap detected: Stomach ↔ Cloaca.\n\nNow, let me finalize analysis.py with the new decision rule, confidence, programmatically-generated evidence, and report.md generation, and run it. I'll cleanly rewrite the output section of the script."}}
